                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 28 at 5:33PM MDT until October 28 at 8:15PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
                "description": "At 533 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.25 to 0.75 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to\nbegin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nHondo, Picacho, and Tinnie.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nRio Hondo, Twin Butte Canyon, Chavez Canyon, Rio Bonito, and Casey\nCanyon.",
